/Title (Providing appropriate extinguishing agents in locations where pyrophoric/ combustible materials are stored, handled or processed. Dry sand, dry sodium chloride or soda ashes are the recommended extinguishing agents in case of fire hazards. Some pyrophoric metals react with water or foams and cause explosion. These may require special powders/use of inert gases. In large storage tanks for powders, any unoccupied volume must be filled using nitrogen or inert gases like argon or helium to avoid reaction with air.      Use of moisture-free processing atmosphere, use of a fireproof enclosure, preferably        free from oxygen.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 930 0 R
/Next 1105 0 R
>>
endobj
1105 0 obj
<<
/Title (Processing should be preferably done under inert gas atmosphere.       Use of non-sparking tools during handling operations.      Keeping easily combustible materials \(wood, paper\) away from the powder storage/handling area.)
